Z||000021||FieroGTguy||06-07-2001||03:45 AM||||FieroMaster, that's a rough one...  It took me like 6 hours to cut the mesh sections right.<P>HMM...  If I could get several people to send me the inerts of their tail lights, I could stack the mesh on the template while cutting it.  Each peice requires test fitting + clipping over and over again.  Might be worth it.  <P>Or, perhaps I will just sell them as a kit?  Tail lights are easy enough to open up, and I'll offer a service fee for those that want to ship them to me for great installation.<P>I think I'll make one more fastback set and put it on ebay to get an accurate retail for them, and then go from there.  <P>More and better pictures will be on the way before they hit Ebay.<P>Fieromaster, I'll give you "special" price because you are so kind to send notchback tail lights for experimentation.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
